er users. Is this…"],["39e1feee_8c8c7a33",15,-15,0,"Please fix this WARNING reported by Code Duplication: Duplicate code found. Review for potential refactoring. This block matches lines... Duplicate code found. Review for potential refactoring. This…"],["9a2f2da5_0e4e0ca2",22,-15,1,"nit: I'd suggest putting `NOTIMPLEMENTED()` in these implementations, they don't hit very often but it makes it much easier to diagnose why something isn't working later on."],["1190903e_d6656732",15,-11,1,"What is stored there? can we use a different `GCMStore` implementation that keeps all data in memory?"],["16998f1c_14761322",23,-11,1,"Please add a comment to make it clear why we need to allow this permission for all frames. Would it make sense to add this permission in fuchsia.web API and then allow it only for pages that actually…"],["94b52a1d_ac0906d9",15,-11,0,"How does this work? IIUC push messages are normally delivered to service workers, see https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:content/browser/push_messaging/push_messaging_router.cc;d…"],["a140445d_56e3b770",24,-11,0,"This file hasn't changed. Not sure why it's included in this CL."],["a1615d6a_1b145a62",23,-11,0,"does this function get called for NOTIFICATION permission? Maybe the change in `GetPermissionResultForCurrentDocument` is enough?"],["c9195096_f3bf4791",25,-11,1,"`connect::GetNetworkConnectionTracker()` keeps the ownership of the result, so we cannot put it in a `unique_ptr`. So we don't need `network_connection_tracker_` - just call…"],["8d52d384_7935227a",15,0,1,"nit: comments like this are usually formatted without spaces, e.g. `/*is_valid=*/false` . https://source.chromium.org/search?q=%22%3D*%2F%22"]],0,643],[7180189,20416,5,0.242,0.169,[[11,8]],[],0,644],[7205586,20417,3,0.09,0.035,[[18,29]],[],0,645],[7181683,20418,118,2.202,1.731,[[11,0.984,9,117],[8,0.016,119,1]],[["5298bd0b_be5281fd",23,-1,1,"Would it make sense to put this in `GetPermissionResultForWorker()` since it's specific to workers?"],["d268df77_434a2459",6,-1,0,"Is this a still valid TODO?"],["e7b7295b_de0c98b7",23,-1,1,"It looks wrong that we apply Service-worker specific flags in a context that's not related to service workers. Maybe remove this?"],["34d375e8_f91d4d74",23,0,1,"nit: ``` return AllowNotifications(worker_origin) ? content::PermissionResult(blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::GRANTED : content::PermissionResult(blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::DENIED ```"]],0,646],[7205795,20425,5,0.422,0.283,[[38,1]],[["64b8b3aa_1fcdb49d",26,-1,1,"nit: Remove this or replace it with just a link to the bug?"]],0,647],[7224282,20425,10,0.399,0.286,[[11,10]],[],0,648],[6892094,20425,5,0.363,0.27,[[17,22]],[],0,649],[7205666,20426,80,0.906,0.686,[[3,0.771,72,62],[5,0.229,63,18]],[],0,650],[7227621,20427,22,0.759,0.477,[[17,0.667,23,15],[39,0.333,1,7]],[],0,651],[7242834,20432,260,6.536,5.29,[[20,0.695,5,180],[19,0.305,7,80]],[],0,652]]}